     "t": "cover",
     "kicker": "Durga Puja · UNESCO",
     "title": "Why UNESCO listed Kolkata's Durga Puja",
     "bn": "ইউনেস্কোর তালিকায় কলকাতার পুজো",
     "sub": "Intangible cultural heritage since December 2021",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Durga_Puja_Festival_-_Kolkata_October_2025.jpg",
      "artist": "Pramanikshreya",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.45
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "What happened",
     "title": "December 2021",
     "bn": "২০২১-এর ডিসেম্বর",
     "body": "UNESCO inscribed \"Durga Puja in Kolkata\" on its Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, on a nomination by India."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Not a World Heritage Site",
     "title": "A living practice, not a place",
     "bn": "জায়গা নয়, জীবন্ত ঐতিহ্য",
     "body": "World Heritage covers places such as the Sundarbans. This list covers living practice. What's recognised isn't a pandal or an image, made and immersed each year, but the practice itself."
    },
    {
     "t": "list",
     "kicker": "Why Kolkata's puja",
     "title": "What UNESCO saw",
     "bn": "কেন কলকাতার পুজো",
     "items": [
      [
       "Made by neighbourhood committees",
       "পাড়ার কমিটির হাতে গড়া"
      ],
      [
       "Image-makers, dhakis, pandal builders, cooks",
       "কারিগর, ঢাকি, প্যান্ডেল শিল্পী"
      ],
      [
       "Public pandals open to anyone",
       "সবার জন্য খোলা প্যান্ডেল"
      ],
      [
       "Brings people together across religion",
       "সব ধর্মের মানুষ একসঙ্গে"
      ],
      [
       "Across caste, class and gender too",
       "জাত, শ্রেণি, লিঙ্গ পেরিয়ে"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "What it does",
     "title": "Recognition, not a law",
     "bn": "স্বীকৃতি, আইন নয়",
     "body": "UNESCO gets no control over the festival, and the listing brings no regular funding by itself. It does commit India to safeguarding the tradition and reporting on how it is faring."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Living heritage",
     "title": "It is meant to change",
     "bn": "ঐতিহ্যও বদলায়",
     "body": "A theme pandal made of recycled materials is as much a part of what UNESCO recognised as an ekchala image in an old family courtyard."
    },
    {
     "t": "photo",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/Maa_Durga_Pandal_Bengal_Culture_Theme.jpg",
      "artist": "Himadri8991",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.45
     },
     "line": "Theme pandals: an open-air exhibition for millions of visitors"
    },
    {
     "t": "end",
     "title": "Our pujo, humanity's heritage",
     "bn": "আমাদের পুজো, মানবতার ঐতিহ্য",
     "ask": "Send it to a friend abroad"
    }
   ],
   "caption": {
    "en": "Why UNESCO recognised Durga Puja in Kolkata as intangible cultural heritage in December 2021 🌏\n\nIt isn't a World Heritage Site; those are places. Durga Puja in Kolkata is on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, which recognises living practice: the image-makers' knowledge, the rituals, the music and the way neighbourhoods run the festival.\n\nThe listing is recognition, not a law. It brings no control and no regular funding by itself, but it commits India to safeguarding the tradition, artisans' livelihoods included.\n\nSend this to a friend who still calls it a World Heritage Site 🙏",
    "keywords": [
     "durga puja unesco",
     "durga puja intangible cultural heritage",
     "unesco heritage durga puja kolkata",
     "intangible cultural heritage india"
    ],
    "tags": "#DurgaPuja #UNESCO #KolkataDurgaPuja"
   }
