     "t": "cover",
     "kicker": "Recipe · Serves 4",
     "title": "Gobindobhog payesh, the sweet end of bhog",
     "bn": "গোবিন্দভোগ চালের পায়েস",
     "sub": "Rice, full-fat milk, bay leaf and cardamom",
     "photo": {
      "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Kheer%28Payasam%29.jpg",
      "artist": "Ayshamarjana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "cx": 0.5,
      "cy": 0.45
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "list",
     "kicker": "Ingredients",
     "title": "What you need",
     "bn": "যা যা লাগবে",
     "items": [
      [
       "1 litre full-fat milk",
       "১ লিটার ঘন দুধ"
      ],
      [
       "¼ cup (50 g) gobindobhog rice",
       "গোবিন্দভোগ চাল"
      ],
      [
       "1 tsp ghee",
       "ঘি"
      ],
      [
       "1 bay leaf",
       "তেজপাতা"
      ],
      [
       "3 green cardamom pods, lightly crushed",
       "থেঁতো এলাচ"
      ],
      [
       "⅓ cup (70 g) sugar, or to taste",
       "চিনি"
      ],
      [
       "10 to 12 cashews, halved, and 1 tbsp raisins",
       "কাজু আর কিশমিশ"
      ],
      [
       "A small pinch of salt",
       "এক চিমটে নুন"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Method",
     "num": 1,
     "title": "Wash, dry, coat",
     "bn": "চাল ধুয়ে ঘি মাখান",
     "body": "Wash the rice in two changes of water, drain and spread it on a plate to dry for 15 minutes. Rub it with the ghee so the grains are lightly coated."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Method",
     "num": 2,
     "title": "Boil, then simmer",
     "bn": "দুধ ফুটিয়ে চাল দিন",
     "body": "Boil the milk with the bay leaf and cardamom in a wide, heavy pan. Add the rice, lower to low-medium and simmer 30 to 35 minutes, scraping every 2 to 3 minutes, till the rice breaks when pressed."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Method",
     "num": 3,
     "title": "Sugar goes in last",
     "bn": "চিনি একদম শেষে",
     "body": "Add the sugar and salt and stir 8 to 10 minutes on low heat. Sugar slows the rice softening, so never add it early. Stir in the cashews and raisins for 2 minutes, then take out the bay leaf."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Method",
     "num": 4,
     "title": "Let it rest",
     "bn": "একটু জিরোতে দিন",
     "body": "Let it stand 15 minutes before offering; it thickens a lot as it cools. Serve warm, at room temperature or chilled. Covered in the fridge, it keeps up to 3 days."
    },
    {
     "t": "step",
     "kicker": "Later in the year",
     "title": "The nolen gur version",
     "bn": "নলেন গুড়ের পায়েস",
     "body": "In winter, from around November to January, leave out the sugar. Turn off the heat, wait 5 minutes and stir in about ½ cup grated nolen gur. Don't boil it again, or the milk may split."
    },
    {
     "t": "end",
     "title": "Save this for Ashtami bhog",
     "bn": "অষ্টমীর ভোগের জন্য রেখে দিন",
     "ask": "Save it with the khichuri recipe"
    }
   ],
   "caption": {
    "en": "Payesh recipe: gobindobhog rice kheer, the sweet that closes the Durga Puja bhog plate 🍚\n\nGobindobhog rice, simmered slowly in full-fat milk with bay leaf, cardamom and sugar until creamy. It serves four. Keep to about 50 g of rice for a litre of milk and it stays pourable.\n\nThere's one rule we'd never break. Cook the rice fully before the sugar goes in, because sugar slows the softening. Then turn off the heat while it still looks a little thin; it thickens as it stands.\n\nSave this for Ashtami 🙏",
